+## F-23 Consumer Boundary
+
+- `vendor/tend-ui/compensation-policy.json` pins checksums, exports and advisory dispositions for all three local compensations;
+- `npm run verify:tend-ui:security` checks integrity, local lock sources, private metadata and security-relevant behavior;
+- `npm run verify:tend-ui:bundle` enforces the current direct-file build boundary and size limits;
+- `npm run verify:tend-ui:all` rebuilds the application and runs every Tend UI integration gate.
+
+Bundle splitting was evaluated and deliberately deferred. The production plugin emits a classic deferred script so `dist/index.html` remains directly openable through `file://`; ordinary Vite dynamic chunks would reintroduce an ES-module loading requirement. The current single bundle is accepted while it stays below `800 KiB` raw and `250 KiB` gzip.
